================= AI-Driven Ansible Automation demo is ready =================

Access
  AAP            https://{{ control_public_ip }}          {{ aap_admin_user }}
  Gitea          {{ gitea_url_external }}          {{ gitea_admin_user }}
  Mattermost     http://{{ control_public_ip }}:{{ mattermost_port }}     {{ mattermost_admin_user }}
  Webserver      http://{{ target_public_ip }}

AI inference
  Endpoint       {{ ai_model_url }}
  Model          {{ ai_model_id }}
  Generation     {{ 'hosted Ansible Lightspeed' if lightspeed_mode == 'saas' else 'demo model endpoint' }}

Created in AAP
  Inventory      {{ demo_inventory_name }} ({{ demo_target_hostname }})
  Projects       {{ demo_project_name }}, {{ demo_playbook_project_name }}
  Workflows      {{ enrichment_workflow_name }}
                 {{ remediation_workflow_name }}
  Activation     {{ eda_activation_name }} -> {{ kafka_topic }}@{{ control_private_ip }}:{{ kafka_port }}

Run the demo
  1. Launch "{{ jt_break_apache }}" in Automation Execution > Templates.
  2. Watch Automation Decisions > Rulebook Activations pick up the Kafka event.
  3. "{{ enrichment_workflow_name }}" runs automatically.
     Check Mattermost #{{ mattermost_channel }} for the logs and the AI RCA.
  4. Launch "{{ remediation_workflow_name }}", review the AI prompt in the
     survey, and finish. The generated playbook is committed to
     {{ gitea_url_external }}/{{ gitea_admin_user }}/{{ demo_playbook_repo }}
  5. Launch "{{ jt_execute_remediation }}" with limit {{ demo_target_hostname }}.
  6. Confirm http://{{ target_public_ip }} is serving again.

Reset between runs
  Launch "{{ jt_restore_apache }}".

==============================================================================
